{"answer":"Under the Constitution in the library, the President is elected by votes cast in a presidential election. If more than two candidates run, the winner must receive the **highest number of votes nationwide** and at least **25% of the votes in each of at least two-thirds of the states and the Federal Capital Territory, Abuja**. [9fd67df7-f4db-4611-92dd-351d376b5dca]

If there are exactly two candidates, the winner must receive a **majority of the votes cast** and meet the same 25% geographical requirement. [f62b33be-ade8-4b08-a98a-2c895d407cc9]

If no candidate meets the requirements, the Constitution provides for another election between two candidates. [9fd67df7-f4db-4611-92dd-351d376b5dca, 7e092889-15b1-4af7-baa5-e3cba2079fd2]","citation_ids":["9fd67df7-f4db-4611-92dd-351d376b5dca","f62b33be-ade8-4b08-a98a-2c895d407cc9","7e092889-15b1-4af7-baa5-e3cba2079fd2"]}
